# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# spec-spine writes wall-clock metadata here. It is the one non-deterministic
# artifact, excluded from every determinism and golden check, so it must never
# be committed.
.derived/**/build-meta.json

# NOT ignored, deliberately: .derived/spec-registry/ and .derived/codebase-index/
# are the committed shard trees. Committing them is what makes `spec-spine check`
# a freshness gate on a pull request: CI compares the corpus against what the
# branch committed.

# The CLI's own runtime state inside a governed repository (spec 002). Managed
# bytes are declared in .statecraft/environment.json, which IS committed; the
# run state, worktrees and records under .statecraft/state/ are not.
.statecraft/state/

# The repository-local spec-spine, installed by `make tools` from the exact
# `required_version` in spec-spine.toml. It is deliberately NOT a shared
# `~/.cargo/bin` install: one binary on PATH is replaced by whichever project
# built it last, and a governed read then either refuses on the pin or, worse,
# answers under a version this repository never adopted.
.tooling/
